{"uncertainty": 0.3, "outcome": "Rewrote the irq_ctrl verification plan as strict JSON in irq_ctrl_vplan.json. Attempt 1 [run:run-0001] failed with 'line 1: Expecting value', which is a JSON parse error: line 1 of the YAML file was a '#' comment. The new plan quotes all 14 [req:...] requirements of the approved spec [artifact:prj-1206fbd80a.interface-spec.a1] word for word and gives each at least one test, assertion and coverage item. It serves [requirement:req-5fc7831312].", "artifacts": [], "files": [{"path": "irq_ctrl_vplan.json", "kind": "verification_plan", "title": "irq_ctrl verification plan (JSON)", "summary": "Verification plan for irq_ctrl, serving [requirement:req-5fc7831312]. It covers all 14 requirements tagged in the approved interface_spec.md [artifact:prj-1206fbd80a.interface-spec.a1]: IRQ-PARAM, IRQ-RESET, IRQ-REG-RW, IRQ-READ, IRQ-LEVEL, IRQ-EDGE, IRQ-DETECT-DISABLED, IRQ-W1C, IRQ-ACK, IRQ-SET-WINS, IRQ-MASK, IRQ-PRIORITY, IRQ-CLAIM and IRQ-LATENCY. Each requirement is quoted exactly and mapped to test, assertion and coverage_point items. The file is strict JSON with no comments, to fix the parse failure in [run:run-0001]. It records no results.", "entry": null}], "tool_runs": ["run:run-0001"], "claims": ["The 'Expecting value' error in [run:run-0001] suggests vplan.check parses plan files as JSON. The plan was therefore converted from YAML with comments to strict JSON and keeps the same top-level fields: block, requirements and items.", "Coverage items name irq_ctrl.sv as the design file. I assume this is the file name of the existing RTL; I have not read the repository to confirm it.", "Test items assume a testbench file irq_ctrl_tb.sv and assertion items assume a bind file irq_ctrl_sva.sv. Neither file exists yet."], "escalation": null, "notes": "Changes from attempt 1:\n(1) The format is now JSON. The header comments and the N = 2/8/32 sweep note are no longer comments; the sweep is stated in item descriptions.\n(2) t_smoke now drops src[0] before the acknowledge. Under IRQ-SET-WINS, acknowledging a level source while its input is high leaves it pending, so the old order contradicted the spec.\n(3) t_ack sets PENDING through the sources and then holds them low. Ids >= N are only reachable for N < 32.\n(4) t_mode_switch now checks only edges after the MODE write. The spec does not say which mode applies at the write edge itself. This is a spec gap the reviewer should raise with architecture.\n\nThe independent review requirement still needs a review_record from another seat. Every requirement has at least one item, so there should be no 'no item yet' lines."}

